   "stem": {
      "text": "Suppose \\( \\int_{1}^{4} f(x)\\,dx = 8 \\) and \\( \\int_{1}^{8} f(x)\\,dx = -5 \\). The function h is defined by \\( h(x) = -2 \\) for \\( x < 7 \\) and \\( h(x) = -4 \\) for \\( x \\ge 7 \\). Find \\( \\int_{8}^{4} \\left(2f(x) + h(x)\\right)\\,dx \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 36
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Split the interval at x = 4: \\( \\int_{4}^{8} f(x)\\,dx = -5 - 8 = -13 \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "additivity over adjacent intervals"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "h jumps at x = 7, so split its integral there: \\( -2 \\cdot 3 - 4 \\cdot 1 = -10 \\).",
         "rule_named": "integral of a step function split at the jump"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "By linearity, \\( \\int_{4}^{8} \\left(2f(x) + h(x)\\right)\\,dx = 2(-13) - 10 = -36 \\).",
         "rule_named": "constant multiple and sum properties"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The requested limits run from 8 down to 4, which changes the sign: the value is \\( 36 \\).",
